# Chapter 4 - Intune's Capabilities in Analytics and Automation
# From the book "AI, Automation and Analytics - Transforming Device Management
# with Intune" (2nd Edition) by Jannik Reinhard.
# https://github.com/JayRHa/intune-aaa-book-code
#
# When you need several small pieces of data at once - the kind of tenant-summary
# dashboard the Intune home page builds - do not fire ten sequential requests.
# Use the Graph $batch endpoint to send them as one round trip. Graph returns an
# array of responses keyed by your "id" values. Easier on the throttle budget and
# noticeably faster. Use id-based "dependsOn" when one call must run after
# another; for read-only summaries you usually want them parallel.

@graph = https://graph.microsoft.com

### One request, three sub-requests
POST {{graph}}/v1.0/$batch
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "requests": [
    {
      "id": "complianceSummary",
      "method": "GET",
      "url": "/deviceManagement/deviceCompliancePolicyDeviceStateSummary"
    },
    {
      "id": "subscriptionState",
      "method": "GET",
      "url": "/deviceManagement/subscriptionState"
    },
    {
      "id": "failedApps",
      "method": "POST",
      "url": "/deviceManagement/reports/getFailedMobileAppsSummaryReport",
      "body": { "filter": "" },
      "headers": { "Content-Type": "application/json" }
    }
  ]
}
